(D8: Discrepancy 8 repro, RESOLVED 2026-10-17 by vox #305: two lists or
 two maps now compare by their contents (LANGUAGE.md:2065-2068), so two
 lists built from the identical literal are equal, and so are two
 identical maps. A list compared against its own rendering as a TEXT still
 compiles with no diagnostic and answers not equal, so that shape is still
 no oracle; the element-wise reads are unchanged.
 Until vox #305 `is equal to` on two collections compiled and always
 answered "not equal" (pointer equality), which made every
 whole-collection assertion in this ledger unavailable.
 Re-recorded 2026-10-17 on vox cb407f8.
